WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Times 10. Does the decimal point jump?

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.160
Look closer. Every seat is worth ten of the seat to its right.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.950
So times 10 moves every digit one seat left.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.730
The point stayed exactly where it was. Only the digits moved.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:20.840
3.45 times 10 is 34.5.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:28.010
Divide by 10, and every digit slides back one seat. 3.45 again.
